Document that ISession::loadModule and its siblings return a module the session owns.

loadModule, loadModuleFromSource, loadModuleFromIRBlob and loadModuleFromSourceString return an
IModule* that the session keeps (getLoadedModuleCount and getLoadedModule enumerate it), and the
caller receives no reference: the pointer is borrowed. Every other ISession call that hands out an
object does so through an out-parameter that carries a reference, and the declarations in slang.h
say nothing about ownership. A caller following the COM convention releases the module once too
often; glibc then aborts (free(): corrupted unsorted chunks), while the Windows heap tolerates it.

This adds one sentence to each of the four declarations. It changes no code.
